        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "title": "ぢ and づ",
          "text": "ぢ and づ sound identical to じ and ず. They appear almost only in compound words (はなぢ nosebleed, つづく to continue) or after a doubled ち/つ (ちぢむ to shrink). じ is used in nearly all other cases (じかん time, じしょ dictionary).",
          "tone": "info"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Yōon (拗音): contracted sounds",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Take an i-row character (き, し, ち, に, ひ, み, り, ぎ, じ, ぢ, び, ぴ) and add a small や, ゆ, or よ (ゃ ゅ ょ). The small kana is written at roughly half size in the lower-right area of the square. Total: 36 combinations (21 unvoiced + 15 voiced / semi-voiced)."
          ]
        },
